WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.407
In under two minutes, you will change your contest's dates and details.

00:00:04.407 --> 00:00:05.520
We start on the map.

00:00:06.423 --> 00:00:09.755
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:11.538 --> 00:00:13.960
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.450
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:17.796
Tap Use my location.

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.766
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:21.766 --> 00:00:22.418
Tap Allow.

00:00:25.958 --> 00:00:28.454
Look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:28.454 --> 00:00:29.672
See the three dots?

00:00:29.672 --> 00:00:30.219
Tap them.

00:00:31.823 --> 00:00:33.785
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:35.479 --> 00:00:36.107
Tap Mine.

00:00:36.107 --> 00:00:38.056
These are the contests you run.

00:00:39.736 --> 00:00:41.758
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:00:41.758 --> 00:00:43.126
This is your dashboard.

00:00:45.013 --> 00:00:47.310
On the Overview, find Schedule.

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:48.531
Tap Change dates.

00:00:50.411 --> 00:00:53.592
Change the date that entries close, and the voting dates.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:01.452
You can also change the name, the message, the prize, and the rules.

00:01:01.452 --> 00:01:03.387
Entrants see changes right away.

00:01:04.288 --> 00:01:05.515
Tap Save changes.

00:01:05.515 --> 00:01:09.467
The team is emailed about changes, so nobody is surprised.

00:01:11.401 --> 00:01:13.271
Next up: Run voting.
